WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guests tonight
are the stars of

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Law &amp; Order: SVU,"
which returns

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.872 line:92%
for its 20th season, Thursday,

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:08.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
September 27th, at 9:00 p.m.,
here on NBC.

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.710 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:12.846 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I got winded...

00:00:12.846 --> 00:00:18.418 size:88% position:44%
chasing that Conway kid,
and I -- I had to stop.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now an innocent woman
who's riding her bike

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
has a broken leg because of --
because of me.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:26.026 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And no matter how much
you suck for air,

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
you couldn't fill your lungs.
-That's right.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:32.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And your legs felt like lead.
-Bingo.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:33.566 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Welcome to the club.

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:38.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
Liv, no one expects you
to be Wonder Woman.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.040 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I do.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:42.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and I used to think
I was Superman.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.910 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-So what happened, then?

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.046 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Life.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.080 line:92%
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
our friends Mariska Hargitay
and Ice-T, everybody.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.652 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.652 --> 00:01:02.729 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:10.737 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:12.605 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Welcome, you two!

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.707
I'm thrilled to have you.
That was a perfect clip.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:18.111
Because you are now in your
20th season of this show,

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:21.281
and now it's only fair that
you would be police officers

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:24.484
who are also a little bit older.
-A little bit.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.351 line:92%
What was fun about this show

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
is we didn't have to bring
our walkers on.

00:01:27.654 --> 00:01:28.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much.
It's just very hard.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.491 line:92%
We never know where to put them.

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, 'cause it would be
awkward.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:33.793 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-So, 20 years of a show.

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, it's still
very appealing

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:36.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
for us as an audience
to watch it.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:41.101
Is it still as appealing for
you guys to do it in season 20?

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:45.538 size:81% position:41%
-I got to say, for me,
it's getting better.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:46.806 size:78% position:39% line:92%
We're having more fun

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
and going deeper
and more invested.

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's pretty incredible
right now.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:53.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think the best thing
about our show is,

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:56.916
everybody on our show that we
work with is so wonderful.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:59.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's easy.
You know, I love Mariska.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.587 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We got along.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:03.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just the work environment
is so fun.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:04.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it doesn't seem
like 20 years.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:05.625 line:92%
It just seems like, you know,

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.193
you're going to work,
doing something you love to do.

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:10.497
-And people throw the word,
you know, "family" around.

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
But after 20 years...
-Yeah.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Well, that's the real deal.

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's true.
And it's the real deal.

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:17.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so...
-And did you --

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.439
Were you two
familiar with each other at all

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:21.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
20 years ago, before you got
teamed up on the show?

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, not at all.
-But it was kind of odd.

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
We used to --
Well, trip off this.

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:29.382
We both lived --
We could see each other's house

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
from where we lived
in Los Angeles,

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.652 line:92%
but we didn't know each other.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
Mariska lived up the hill

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:36.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little higher than me,
of course.

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.223 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.993
But she would
come down the hill, and then --

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'd be driving up, going,
"That's Ice-T's house.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.396 size:81% position:41% line:92%
That's Ice-T's house."

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:45.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it was just odd.
It was weird.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:47.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
And here we are together.
-Yeah. Meant to be.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.838
-I heard you refer to Ice
in interviews and articles

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:54.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a philosopher king.
-Completely.

00:02:54.007 --> 00:02:56.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is there advice
he's imparted upon you over --

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:57.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's so much advice,
but it's daily.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
And first of all, you know,
we all get in our --

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're all in our little worlds
that we live in,

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:04.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I've never seen,
in 20 years,

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:08.555
this man come to work
in a bad mood, not be grateful,

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:11.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
always ready to work,
always ready.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.292 size:81% position:41% line:92%
He's never complained.

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:13.226 line:92%
I've never heard him complain.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:14.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everyone complains.
Who doesn't complain?

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
I complain.
And he never complains.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:21.401
But, also, I think your gift
is that he has the ability,

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:24.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
no matter what
we're talking about,

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:27.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
to distill it down
to its purest essence.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I just believe
everybody needs

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:32.478
a reference point to [bleep] up,
all right?

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.012 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:36.416 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if you can --
When you're on a set --

00:03:36.416 --> 00:03:37.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're on a set.
We're making movies,

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:41.120
and you can feel bad, but I've
been through some bad things,

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.122 size:75% position:38%
so I always use that
as a reference point

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:46.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be like, "Shut up. Relax.
You're lucky.

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're fortunate."
And then --

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You're on a TV show.
-Yeah.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you're acting.
-Sitting with Seth.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know what I'm saying?
You got fans.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:52.999 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Like, what?

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:55.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
You got a lot of nerve
to be upset.

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:56.536 line:92%
So I just bring it right back.

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:59.439
And then I try to transfer that
to everybody on the set.

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:01.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, "Look,
we're all very lucky,

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:03.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
and let's just be blessed,
you know?

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:04.777 line:92%
And take advantage of it."

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.279 --> 00:04:08.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is the truth.
-That's great philosophy.

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That is the truth.
That is the truth.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What was --
Was there anything

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:14.354
that was surprising to you
about Mariska over the years

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:15.388 line:92%
that you maybe didn't expect?

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:17.323
-Well, I think when people
watch her on television,

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:20.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
she very rarely does anything
funny on our show.

00:04:20.793 --> 00:04:22.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's always so ser--
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:23.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right?
-By the way, that's good.

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:26.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There's so much opportunity.
-Yeah, I was gonna say.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:28.534
"You know,
that was a really funny episode

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.036 line:92%
of 'Special Victims Unit.'"

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:32.405 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:33.573 line:92%
-Hey, I'm just telling you.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:35.108 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
I watch her on television,

00:04:35.108 --> 00:04:37.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm like, "Wow, wow,
she's dead serious."

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:39.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
But behind the scenes,
she's crazy.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:42.415 size:78% position:39%
She's fun to be with.
Nothing but jokes.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:45.118 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not even jokes we can even
tell on television.

00:04:45.118 --> 00:04:46.853 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:50.456
-Did you --
Do you ever listen Ice's music?

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do.
-Yeah, that's great.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:53.126 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-We share everything.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:56.396
So he'll come, and he's so cute.
He's like a little kid.

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like,
"Look at my new video,"

00:04:58.131 --> 00:05:00.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, "Listen my new song."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know --
-Why is that funny?

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I just don't think
a lot of people

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.738 line:92%
think of Body Count as cute.

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:06.506 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:07.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
But I know him differently.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah, she knows me.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.311
-Well, there was one thing cute
about a recent Body Count show.

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:13.379
You were in Switzerland, right?
-Yeah.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.014 line:92%
-And you were doing a show.

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.215 line:92%
And your daughter, Chanel,

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:18.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
was on stage
while you were performing.

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:21.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that is something
you don't expect to see.

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:22.655 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:24.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's her fake mic.
She got a mic.

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:26.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
She gets onstage,
and she rocks out.

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.361 line:92%
She's not afraid of the crowd.

00:05:28.361 --> 00:05:29.195 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And, you know, it's --

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:31.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, at the end of the day,
this is entertainment.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:32.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
My man over there
from Alice in Chains know.

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:35.168
If you're not having fun,
you're missing the point.

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:36.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know, that's what it is.

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:37.403 line:92%
-And what does the audience --

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are they surprised
when a child walks on stage?

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do they feel like
something's gone wrong or...?

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
what I do in the show,

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:45.378
I usually ask who's the youngest
person in the audience.

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:48.281
And they're usually like 12,
and I say, "I got you beat,"

00:05:48.281 --> 00:05:49.949 line:92%
and out comes a 2-year-old.

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:52.051 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.052 line:92%
-You were traveling, as well.

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:54.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think you were
in Switzerland, as well.

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:55.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was.
-This is your husband.

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:57.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow, we're whipping out
the Instagram.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:05:59.025 --> 00:05:59.592 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:01.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is that --
-"Just making some bratwurst."

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:04.130
-Yeah, he is -- he's grilling up
his own bratwurst.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:04.530 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He was.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is he handy like that
on a trip?

00:06:06.532 --> 00:06:08.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was this day.
-Okay.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.102 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.102 --> 00:06:11.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
So this is not
a normal occurrence?

00:06:11.003 --> 00:06:12.705 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no.
Well, no.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:13.539 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
No.
He can grill.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:18.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah?
That's really lovely.

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, he actually cooks
more than I do.

00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:21.948 size:84% position:42%
This was a special day.
And I have to tell say,

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:24.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
this was, I think,
my favorite day

00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:26.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
of our whole
month-long vacation.

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:26.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:06:26.853 --> 00:06:28.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that's great.
-It was very beautiful.

00:06:28.788 --> 00:06:29.455 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-It looks beautiful.

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's a handsome guy
with a good vacation beard.

00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:32.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
if that's full-time,

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:33.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that looks like
a vacation beard to me.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's full time.
It's anytime he's not working.

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:36.329 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay, gotcha.

00:06:36.329 --> 00:06:37.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And his hair
looks like a hedgehog.

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:40.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I enjoy it.
-So, the other interes--

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:41.033 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:41.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What?
Was that weird?

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:44.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, I think it's good.
Look, get it out there.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let people
know something about you.

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:49.108 size:75% position:38%
-Peter will tell you
what happened later.

00:06:49.108 --> 00:06:50.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.943 --> 00:06:54.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm just saying -- whatever.
Okay.

